<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 24.78 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 24.78 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 93 basis points to 24.78 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     25.71	    24.78		   - 93 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     25.99	    25.22		   - 77 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    25.64	    25.46		   - 18 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     25.98	    25.75		   - 23 bps</p>
<p>The results of the auction will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559</p>
</text>
